# Gelse (M5, D-079): a Salzkammergut summer mosquito. Slim dark body d with
# an m-striped abdomen and a k outline on the body only, long 1 px d legs, a
# k needle with an r tip, blurred wings h w (no outline).
# fly = wing blur (frame 0 up, frame 1 down/back), the body stays.
# wait = the telegraph: same wings, 1 px side-to-side wiggle and w whine dashes.
# leave = nose up, a small round r belly: full. squished = flattened, w star.
# Faces right, mirror = auto. Hitbox 8x8 centred at sprite (8,8).
# Built with a scratch script (shapes + automatic k outline), frozen here.
sprite = gelse
size   = 16x16
origin = 8,12
hitbox = 4,4,8,8
mirror = auto
anim   = fly       frames=2 ticks=2 loop
anim   = wait      frames=2 ticks=4 loop
anim   = leave     frames=1
anim   = squished  frames=1
